{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"alias":"free-slothful-fennecfox","creation_channel":"cli","description":"## Summary\n\nSibling read/CLI entry points still gate initialization on a bare `os.path.isdir(tracker)`,\nthe exact defect fixed for the library/MCP read chokepoint in `rapt-dreadable-dromedary`\n(aefe-614a-2631-4117). A tracker directory that EXISTS but is not a usable store (no `.git`,\nor `.git` with an unresolvable HEAD mid-clone) satisfies `isdir`, so these paths report\n\"initialized\" (or return empty) for a broken/mid-clone store instead of `store_uninitialized`.\n\nDiscovered during the rebar-debug Step 7 parity sweep for `rapt-dreadable-dromedary`. That fix\nwas deliberately scoped to the in-process library/MCP read path (`_reads._tracker`) plus the\nshared write gate; the CLI/read-support parity was scoped OUT by the operator and is filed here.\n\n## Sites (bare `os.path.isdir(tracker)` init gates)\n\n- `src/rebar/_engine_support/reads_cli.py:340` (list) and `:384` (recent-session-logs) — the CLI\n  read path; prints \"ticket system not initialized\" only when the dir is absent.\n- `src/rebar/_engine_support/descendants.py:25`\n- `src/rebar/_engine_support/next_batch.py:153` (`if tracker and os.path.isdir(tracker)`)\n- `src/rebar/_snapshot/repo_snapshot.py:619`\n- `src/rebar/_engine_support/reads.py:245` (`tracker_abs`) — assess whether it funnels through\n  the same guard or needs its own.\n\n## Suggested approach\n\nReuse the shared predicate introduced by the parent fix,\n`rebar._store.store_usability.store_is_usable(tracker)`, at each site (it is stdlib-only and\nalready the read/write source of truth for `.git` + resolvable HEAD). Keep the empty-but-\ninitialized-store contract (`[]` / exit 0). Add parity regression tests mirroring\n`tests/unit/test_reads_uninitialized_store.py` (present-but-`.git`-less and mid-clone stores).\n\n## Acceptance criteria\n\n- [ ] Each listed site rejects a present-but-unusable store (no `.git` / mid-clone) rather than\n      treating it as initialized/empty.\n- [ ] An existing, empty, INITIALIZED store still succeeds (contract preserved).\n- [ ] Regression coverage per site; guard fails if reverted to bare `os.path.isdir`.","id":"be80-8377-4b4c-44f4","parent_id":"","priority":2,"tags":[],"ticket_type":"bug","title":"CLI/read-support init gates still use bare isdir(tracker) — parity with rapt-dreadable-dromedary"},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"CREATE","timestamp":1787961264112914001,"uuid":"bfedc5be-a571-4689-9d25-b60c0e0acbb9"}